concepts.def:
Definition and Core Idea: A recurrence relation is an equation that defines a sequence where each term is given as a
function of its preceding terms. They are fundamental in algorithm analysis (e.g., complexity of recursive algorithms),
combinatorics (e.g., Fibonacci numbers), and discrete probability.

qs.text:
An independent set in a graph is a subset of vertices such that no two vertices in the subset are connected
by an edge. An incomplete scheme for a greedy algorithm to ﬁnd a maximum independent set in a tree is
given below:
 V: Set of all vertices in the tree;
 I := ϕ
 while V ≠ ϕ do
 begin
 ▢ select a vertex u ∊ V such that
 ▢ _______;
 ▢ V := V - {u};
 ▢ if u is such that
 ▢ ________then I := I ∪ {u}
 end;
 Output(I);

 A. Complete the algorithm by specifying the property of vertex ▢ in each case.
 B. What is the time complexity of the algorithm?
